# Transmog, the client side of server src-patch 0019 (server/README.md "Transmog"): item custom attribute 8 is the client id of a look the item is drawn with instead of its own (appearance only). Item::draw (map tiles, inventory and container slots, trade, market, drag) and Item::drawToImage use that look's thing type with its own patterns and animation; everything else (getId, flags, stack position, packets, tooltips, light) stays the item's own, so moving, using and trading the item are unchanged. A look that is stackable or a fluid / splash type is ignored. Lua: item:getAppearanceId(), item:setAppearanceId(clientId) (windows that build items from server data, e.g. the market, the inspect window and the Transmog previews). Key in game_itemrarity ChaosItemAttr.APPEARANCE.
